*.pem

# Every env file holds settings, and most of them secrets: .env.production,
# .env.development and any other name included, not only the .local ones.
# The example is the one meant to be shared, and has no values in it.
.env*
!.env.example

npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# Regenerated by `next dev` on every run, so there is nothing to keep.
AGENTS.md

# CLAUDE.md is NOT generated. It is written by hand and it is the first thing
# read when work resumes here, which is the whole reason it exists. It was
# sitting under the rule above and was therefore never committed once, so
# every note left for the next session died with the machine that wrote it.

# Generated review packs
# Generated documents. Both are built from the content rather than being the
# content, so committing them means a stale copy sitting next to a live source
# and somebody eventually reading the wrong one.
review-pack.html
review-pack-*.html
academy-australia.html
academy-malaysia.html
